  "cause": "**A single missile fired overnight from a warplane hit the building holding the surgical wards and the intensive care units of Nasser hospital in Khan Younis, and the largest hospital in the southern Gaza Strip is now a casualty list.** The Hamas-run health ministry says at least **six** were killed and about **twenty** injured, among the dead the surgeon **Dr Rizk Abu Shaira**; eyewitnesses told the **BBC** the missile penetrated the five-storey structure and struck a room in the surgical department, and the hospital's director described a vertical strike with extensive damage. A Civil Defence paramedic who arrived after the strike described smoke inside the building and beds and equipment scattered on the second floor; the agency's spokesman first gave a toll of five dead and twenty injured. The **Israeli military** says it targeted a commander of **Hamas**'s armed wing and other fighters who had used the hospital as a *\"headquarters\"* to plan attacks on its forces; Hamas calls that *\"false narratives\"* in a *\"blatant attempt to cover up a new war crime.\"* Israel does not permit international news organisations, the BBC included, into Gaza — which means the two accounts of what the building was being used for cannot be tested by anyone who is not a party to the war. **The hospital has a record, and the record is the argument.** Nasser was hit by a **double Israeli strike in August 2025** that killed at least **twenty**, including journalists and health workers. A ceasefire has nominally held since **October last year**; more than **1,620** people have been killed since then, according to the territory's health ministry, whose figures the **UN** considers reliable, against more than **74,650** killed since October 2023. And the weather is now doing what the strikes do not: heavy rains have flooded tens of thousands of tents, and at least **four** members of one family died in the camps this week. Israel says Gaza will not be rebuilt until Hamas disarms. **In the same week the political layer stopped agreeing on what happened.** The 26th Knesset seated its **Arrangements Committee** under **Roy Folkman**, and Speaker **Amir Ohana** set the vote on his own replacement for **Tuesday 17 November at 4 p.m.**, on a request bearing **67** signatures. Now **Likud** alleges foreign interference and says Arab-led parties *\"stole\"* the election after its coalition lost its majority; the **Shin Bet** chief has made what Israeli reporters describe as unprecedented allegations about election interference, and Justice **Noam Solberg** certified the elections and said nothing unlawful occurred on Election Day. The security service is also being used against people who explain the arithmetic: **Abed Abu Shehadeh** — Abdel Qader Abu Shehadeh — a Palestinian citizen of Israel who has published in Arabic, English and Hebrew for a decade, was taken from his home in **Jaffa** on the night of **3 November** by police and Shin Bet officers, held five days on suspicion of *\"contacting a foreign agent\"* over an interview published openly on **26 October**, and released on **9 November**. At his hearing a police representative first acknowledged he was a journalist, then retracted after a recess and called him a *\"political adviser.\"* He told **103FM** the point was to frighten Arab citizens and journalists: *\"They are afraid, and they want to frighten us.\"* The **NYT** reported the detention on Thursday; the **CPJ** has documented it.",
