  "hinge": "§3:16 is three clauses and no exceptions — care for the sick, watch for their healing, console the mourning — and it is addressed to the reader, not to a ministry of health. The change available is forensic and therefore cheap: a joint protocol, agreed this month, under which any strike on a hospital is followed within 48 hours by a published record — munition type, trajectory, the floor struck, the names of the dead — and access for the **ICRC** or **WHO** to the site, from whichever side holds the ground. Israel says the building was a command post; that is a testable claim and a state with evidence should want it tested. Hamas says it was a war crime; that is also testable. Neither can be established by a spokesman. The political file has the same shape: hand the Shin Bet material to the Arrangements Committee under a written mandate instead of letting it leak into an election dispute, and the inquiry into 7 October gets terms of reference, a chair and a reporting date before the speaker's vote on 17 November. A house that writes those two pages can still govern. One that does not will spend its first year arguing about whether it was elected."
