  "hinge": "§8:43 puts the whole weight on one verb — *determine through your agreements* — and warns that the window in which rationality still governs is finite: *before it is too late*. An agreement is a text with clauses, and three of them cost no side a metre of ground this week. First, a published joint schedule of protected infrastructure — the refineries struck since late October, the substations and generating plants hit in Ukraine, the ports and the cold chain — with a named verification body and a 30-day reporting cycle; countable, therefore signable. Second, a list of the prisoners to be exchanged, with names and a transfer date, done for its own sake and not announced as momentum. Third, the European seat written into the document rather than requested from Putin: one named representative, named by the Europeans before the next round convenes, so the architecture that Europe must guarantee is drafted by someone who answers to a European parliament. Kushner is right that Europe needs one voice. That is a European decision, not a Russian one, and it can be taken this week."
